@prefix aegis: <http://aegis.gastown.local/ontology/> .
@prefix owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# Scalar identifiers emitted by the repository and episode ingestion paths.
# Quipu's bitemporal write path supersedes an earlier current value when OWL
# validation is enabled; two distinct values in one transaction remain an
# error.  rdfs:label is deliberately absent: it has multiple producers and is
# not an identifier.
aegis:filePath   a owl:FunctionalProperty .
aegis:sha        a owl:FunctionalProperty .
aegis:hash       a owl:FunctionalProperty .
aegis:contentHash a owl:FunctionalProperty .
aegis:groupId    a owl:FunctionalProperty .

# rdfs:comment is deliberately ABSENT, for the same reason rdfs:label is: it has
# multiple producers and is not an identifier.  It was declared functional in
# 10ecb85 on the premise that "a node has one current description".  The deployed
# graph falsifies that premise -- measured 2026-09-12 (aegis-buipvc), 992 entities
# carry more than one current rdfs:comment and 90.3% of them hold GENUINELY
# DISTINCT FACTS rather than successive drafts of one description.  One host
# entity alone carries 46: one names the services and glibc version it runs,
# another describes its network mounts, another records a monitoring quirk --
# different observations by different producers, not one description rewritten.
# A single entity showed ten distinct prov:wasGeneratedBy episodes.
#
# Enforcing functionality over that shape does not tidy the graph, it blocks every
# POST /ontology with 200 violations, and the only conforming repair would close
# 1,690 facts out of the current view.  If one-current-description is still wanted,
# the surplus belongs on a multi-valued annotation predicate first; the axiom can
# return after that migration, not before it.
